  "approximations": [
    "Buffer-hit latency and per-bank FIFO are explicitly configured logical timing.",
    "A buffered hit samples its word at admission; MRAM sampling follows the selected port policy.",
    "Host barriers cancel delayed transfers; this is a logical host operation, not an electrical hardware pulse."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The original BRZ/BRS tags/registers and PhysicalMemory are shared.",
    "Missed operand reads do not populate BRZ; fetched commands never read BRZ.",
    "Old writeback completion cannot delete an identical or different newer BRZ value.",
    "Guest RP writes retain the original prerequisite that guest software publishes BRZ first.",
    "Guest mapping/control-register routing, CPU fetch and accepted-operand binding remain future driver work.",
    "The returned immutable word is a transfer latch, not a complete independently addressed BRCh register bank.",
    "No new hardware OS gate is implied by functional CERN/performance checks."
  ]
}
